## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical ICA design for real-world sensor data, including preprocessing, component selection, and robust validation with ground truth.

## Key Concepts

- ICA basics: whitening, demixing matrix, independence
- Practical choices: batch vs online, model order selection, stability
- Validation: SDR/SIR, reference injections

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo batch ICA flow for 4-sensor data
function batchICA(X, nComponents){
  // X: [4 x N]
  // 1) center
  const Xc = center(X);
  // 2) whiten
  const Xw = whiten(Xc);
  // 3) ICA step (gradient or fixed-point)
  const W = icaGradientStep(Xw, nComponents);
  return W;
}
```

